malachi
Copyright (c) 2026 Daniel Dombrowsky

malachi is a Go port of parts of tau (https://github.com/huggingface/tau), a
Python coding-agent harness that is itself modeled on Pi. Portions of malachi
are derived from tau, including the agent loop and harness, the tool-history
repair, the read/write/edit/bash tool behavior, the system prompt and
compaction prompts, the OpenAI-compatible and Responses API stream handling,
the session and RPC wire formats, and project trust. The test fixtures in
agent/testdata, agent/session/testdata and rpc/testdata were generated by
running tau.

